# --- Artifact policy (see .kiro/steering/artifact-policy.md) ---
# Large raw I/Q must NOT enter Git history. Regenerate from generators + manifests,
# or fetch large canonical datasets externally by checksum. Committing one of these
# requires a deliberate `git add -f` and should be rare and justified.
*.iq
*.iq32
*.lsisiq
*.difi
*.cf32
*.cs16
*.cs8
*.sigmf-data
# Keep small golden packets explicitly (a few KB) — allowlisted below.
# Golden DIFI packets are the shared conformance oracle for every implementation;
# they are small (KB) and MUST be committed, so override the *.difi rule for them.
!tests/golden/
!tests/golden/**
!**/tests/golden/
!**/tests/golden/**

# Build / environment
build/
build-*/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock

# C++ / CMake
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/

# Conformance oracle: fetched DIFI Consortium reference definitions (third-party code,
# fetched on demand by tests/conformance/setup.sh, never redistributed here).
tests/conformance/.difi-cert/

# Signal generator working dir: large regenerated raw I/Q (never committed; the
# committed manifest in signals/ reproduces it on demand).
work/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/

# Internal correspondence drafts — not for the public repo
docs/email-to-*-DRAFT.md
